From ebcbac0fcf24920deb7ee27f7ee3a846c0f299a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:19:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] fix(app): the meridian rapid law judges a boring bar's
 body and a blade's band

Review of PR #135. A Bore tool's body (its radius about the nose, up its
flute and shank) must fit the hole a pilot drilled, not the nose alone:
a 10 mm bar down a 4 mm pilot is convicted, and the turning_bore pilot
is an 11 mm drill. Groove, part and form blades are judged across their
band (the move is the band's centre), a thread across its crest. Arc
feeds credit nothing (a chord is not the sweep), and a drill with no
stated point is read as 118 degrees, not flat.

Fixes #103

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 RECOMMENDED.md                             | 27 +++++++++
 crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs       | 13 ++++
 crates/app/src/operation/turning_rapids.rs | 70 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 crates/app/src/rest.rs                     |  9 ++-
 crates/app/tests/turning_bore.rs           | 37 +++++++++---
 5 files changed, 143 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

